The absolute value graph is lower than or equal to the horizontal line $y=13$ between the intersections at $x=-4$ and $x=9$.
$$\therefore -4\le x\le9$$

$$y=\left|2\left(x+\dfrac{1}{2}\right)\right|-3$$
This is $y=|2x|$ translated left $\dfrac{1}{2}$ and down 3.

